==============================================================================
  Demo 3 -- closed-loop repair using body_offender.needed
==============================================================================

  Loop: eval -> DeltaTrap -> anomaly -> apply suggested patch -> eval -> pass

  program: (conserve 77 (violate 77))
    patched offender `violate` @ path (): 78 -> 77
    patched program evaluates to 77 (conservation holds)

  program: (conserve 10 (merge 7 4))
    patched offender `merge` @ path (): 11 -> 10
    patched program evaluates to 10 (conservation holds)

  program: (conserve 10 (merge (violate 3) 4))
    patched offender `violate` @ path (0,): 4 -> 6
    patched program evaluates to 10 (conservation holds)

  program: (conserve 5 (violate (violate 2)))
    patched offender `violate` @ path (0,): 3 -> 4
    patched program evaluates to 5 (conservation holds)

  program: (conserve 10 7)
    patched offender `lit` @ path (): 7 -> 10
    patched program evaluates to 10 (conservation holds)

==============================================================================
  Experiment 09 -- complete
==============================================================================
  жд-traps now ship with a body_offender field pointing at the
  deepest sub-expression whose single-node replacement closes
  the deviation.  The outer CONSERVE frame is still recorded in
  offending_op (for back-compat); body_offender is the signal
  an AI repair loop actually uses.
